# CLAUDE.md
## Stack & Versions
* Next.js: 15
* SQLite: better-sqlite3
* Node.js: 18.x

## Folder Structure
* `components`: Reusable React components
* `containers`: Components that wrap other components
* `db`: Database schema and migration files
* `lib`: Utility functions
* `models`: Database model definitions
* `pages`: Next.js pages
* `public`: Static assets
* `styles`: Global CSS styles

## SQL / Migration Conventions
* Use `better-sqlite3` for database interactions
* Migrations are stored in `db/migrations`
* Migration files follow the format `YYYYMMDDHHMMSS_description.sql`
* Use `sqlite3` command to run migrations

## Component Patterns
* Use functional components
* Use `React.memo` for memoization
* Use `React.useCallback` for callback functions
* Use `React.useContext` for context API

## Dev Commands
* `npm run dev`: Start development server
* `npm run build`: Build production bundle
* `npm run migrate`: Run database migrations
* `npm run test`: Run unit tests

## Patterns to Follow
* Use `const` for variable declarations
* Use `let` for variable reassignments
* Use template literals for string concatenation
* Use arrow functions for function declarations

## Anti-Patterns to Avoid
* Using `var` for variable declarations
* Using `==` for equality checks
* Using `console.log` for debugging
* Using `setTimeout` for asynchronous operations

## What We Don't Do (and Why)
* We don't use `class` components because they are less efficient than functional components
* We don't use `jQuery` because it is not necessary with modern React
* We don't use `async/await` for synchronous operations because it can lead to unnecessary complexity
